        "comparison": "Both C and GS disclose indemnifications where maximum payouts cannot be estimated due to the unpredictable nature of triggering events, specifically regarding tax law changes. C notes that it 'is not able to estimate the maximum potential amount of future payments... because the triggering events are not predictable' (c_2024_8_P911_S004) in the context of intercompany legal and tax matters. GS similarly states that 'Future changes in tax laws and how such laws would apply to these indemnifications cannot be determined' (gs_2024_8_P530_S004) and that there are no stated amounts (gs_2024_8_P530_S003). Unlike C, which does not quantify risk probability, GS explicitly states that management believes it is 'unlikely the firm will have to make any material payments' (gs_2024_8_P530_S006).",
