        "peer_disclosure_id": "jpm_2024_8_D584",
        "relationship": "same_topic",
        "comparison": "Both C and JPM disclose that maximum exposure under indemnification arrangements is difficult or impossible to estimate due to the unpredictability of future claims or legal changes. C states it 'is not able to estimate the maximum potential amount of future payments... because the triggering events are not predictable' (c_2024_8_P911_S004). JPM agrees that 'It is difficult to estimate the Firm's maximum exposure under these indemnification arrangements, since this would require an assessment of future changes in tax law and future claims that may be made... that have not yet occurred' (jpm_2024_8_P872_S004). Both parties identify tax-related events as a key driver of this uncertainty. JPM, however, assesses the risk of loss as 'remote' based on historical experience (jpm_2024_8_P872_S005), a risk quantification not provided by C.",
